  "scientific_status": "Ordered common-coupling Gaussian-Wick descendants have a constructive fixed-degree moment algorithm and deterministic energy regressions. The cut-diagram no-bridge cancellation and all-external-degree bound give absolutely continuous residual two-energy measures; exact samplewise pinching is then controlled. The established time-series tails yield a convergent neutral finite-time covariance construction. The charged defect, AA/AB/BA and bulk dictionary remain open.",
  "parameters": "Standard CAR, overlapping complex Gaussian p-body, common original J across charges, normalized annealed beta=mu=0 full trace, hbar=1/string real time, even N and lambda_N=p^2/N tending to positive lambda, fixed Js. Polynomial degrees and external real time are fixed before the double-scale limit.",
  "proof_scope": "Finite checks verify complete Gaussian bookkeeping and exact low-degree diagram formulas. They do not by themselves prove the arbitrary-degree spectral bound or energy-pinching limit. Those use the manuscript cut-field argument, Hermite bridge suppression, positive-measure convergence and the predecessor uniform summable tails. The series tail bound is uniform in compact memory times and all external real times; this is not a claim of uniform-in-external-time convergence of the finite-N spectral measures.",
  "continuation": "Compute charged forward/reverse sources and the AA, AB and BA kernels in the same original-J diagram system, recovering the previously nonzero low-order mixed spectral calibration. The saved oriented-transfer seed starts from the exact full-Fock D identity; its proposed weighted whole-exponential limit has not been established in this stage. Then return to the Susskind bulk mass/position dictionary and interaction observables.",
